# No operational data on GitHub

Repo destino: `fabianmelo23/oporto-residencial`  
Producción: `https://oporto-residencial-production.up.railway.app` (data en Volume Railway)

When the user asks to commit / push / sync to GitHub: upload **code changes only**.  
**NADA** de data operativa — ni local ni de producción. NADA significa NADA.

## Tres universos de data (nunca mezclar)

| Universo | Dónde vive | ¿Va a GitHub? |
|----------|------------|---------------|
| Local | `data/database.local.json` | **NUNCA** |
| Producción Railway | Volume `/data/database.json` | **NUNCA** |
| Seed template | `data/database.json` | Solo si el usuario pide explícitamente cambiar el **template vacío/demo**, nunca un dump |

## Do not

- Commit / stage / push `database.local.json`, `database.demo.json`, `database.wipe.json`, `test-database.local.json`, o cualquier `data/database.*.json` runtime
- Copy local DB → `data/database.json` “para sincronizar”
- Copy Railway volume / production dump → `data/database.json` o al repo
- Sync residents, visits, reservations, correspondence, payments, audit logs, notifications, photos, signatures from local or Railway into GitHub
- “Update the seed with my current local/production data” unless the user **explicitly** asks to change the seed **template** itself (not a dump)

## Allowed in commits

- `src/`, `public/`, `test/`, `docs/`, `.cursor/`, `package.json`, `package-lock.json`, `server.js`, `.gitignore`, `.env.example`, README
- `data/database.test-seed.json` only for automated tests
- `data/database.json` only when the user explicitly asks to edit the empty/demo seed template

## Before every commit / push

1. Review `git status` and `git diff --cached`
2. Abort if any runtime DB, `.env`, photos/signatures dump, or production data appears staged
3. If unsure about `data/database.json` → **ask the user first**

Prefer leaving operational data only on the machine (local) or the Railway volume (production).
